## Load and visualize light exposure data for Costa Rica

The `load_data()` function loads pre-processed data from the *MeLiDos* project. The `site` argument can be set to one or multiple sites. In our case, UCR loads the right data. Check above to see details about the site. To reduce data complexity, we use 1-minute aggregated data, which has also been pre-processed and cleaned. 


::: {.cell}

```{.r .cell-code}
data <- load_data("light_chest_1minute", site = site)
#try setting "light_glasses_1minute", or switch to a different site instead
names(data)
```

::: {.cell-output .cell-output-stdout}

